-- The entry for a chapter, by walking the two parallel lists together; NOTHING when the chapter has no entry.
GIVEN chapters IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      entries IS A LIST OF STRING
      chapter IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the entry among` chapters `and` entries `for chapter` chapter MEANS
    CONSIDER chapters
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN first FOLLOWED BY later THEN
            CONSIDER entries
                WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
                WHEN entry FOLLOWED BY otherEntries THEN
                    IF first EQUALS chapter
                    THEN JUST entry
                    ELSE `the entry among` later `and` otherEntries `for chapter` chapter

-- THE STATUS FUNCTION. From a chapter number to what the extract's status table shows for it.
-- A number that is not a whole number from 1 to the last chapter is outside the cc. 1-37 the extract names. That is all this
-- claims: the extract's editorial note says the chapter numbers of the Statute "includes cc. 1-37", which does not close the list,
-- so the constructor says only that the number is not among those the extract names (fork F-NOTCOVERED).
@ref Per-chapter status table of the extract (src:57-84)
GIVEN chapter IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Chapter status`
`the status shown for chapter` chapter MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF chapter LESS THAN 1 THEN `outside the cc. 1-37 the extract names`
        IF chapter GREATER THAN `the last chapter number` THEN `outside the cc. 1-37 the extract names`
        IF NOT (FLOOR chapter EQUALS chapter) THEN `outside the cc. 1-37 the extract names`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the entry among` `the chapters that have a repeal status entry` `and` `the repeal status entries` `for chapter` chapter
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `no repeal annotation shown`
                WHEN JUST entry THEN
                    IF elem chapter `the chapters shown repealed in part`
                    THEN `shown repealed in part` entry
                    ELSE `shown repealed` entry

